      "text": "$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac {4}{3}$\n\nLet's solve the problem step by step, ensuring we use all the required Python code for intermediate computations.\n\nGiven the equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x = 9\\), we can rewrite it as \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\).\n\nLet's denote the roots of the polynomial as \\(r, s,\\) and \\(t\\). According to Vieta's formulas, we can relate the coefficients of the polynomial to the sums and products of its roots:\n- \\(r + s + t = 5\\)\n- \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\)\n- \\(rst = 9\\)\n\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\).\n\nUsing the identity \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rsr + stt + trs}{rst}\\), we can simplify it to:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rt + rt \\cdot rs + rs \\cdot st}{rst} = \\frac{(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st)}{rst}.\n\\]\nWe know:\n\\[\n(rs)(rt) = (rs)^2 = (rs)^2,\n\\]\n\\[\n(rs)(st) = (rs)(st),\n\\]\n\\[\n(rt)(st) = (rt)(st).\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st) = (rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st).\n\\]\nNow we can substitute \\(rst = 9\\):\n\\[\n(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st) = (rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st) = (rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st).\n\\]\nUsing Vieta's formulas, we know \\((rs)(rt) = (rs)^2 = (rs)^2\\), and similarly, \\((rs)(st) = (rs)(st)\\), \\((rt)(st) = (rt)(st)\\). However, since we don't have specific values for \\(rs, rt,\\) and \\(st\\), we need to express it in terms of \\(r, s,\\) and \\(t\\).\n\nSince \\(rst = 9\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st)}{9}.\n\\]\nKnowing that \\(rs + rt + st = 6\\), we can substitute \\(rts = 9\\):\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\right)(rst) = (rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st).\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\frac{(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st)}{rst} = \\frac{(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st)}{9}.\n\\]\nSince the polynomial's roots satisfy the equation, we know:\n\\[\n(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st) = (rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st).\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\right)(9) = \\frac{(rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st)}{9}.\n\\]\nSince \\(rst = 9\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\right) \\cdot 9 = (rs)(rt) + (rs)(st) + (rt)(st).\n\\]\nFinally, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{1}{5}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}.\n\\]\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Given polynomial x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\ncoefficients = [1, -5, 6, -9]\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots = np.roots(coefficients)\n\n# Calculate the expression rs/t + st/r + tr/s\nrs_over_t = roots[0] * roots[2]\nst_over_r = roots[1] * roots[2]\ntr_over_s = roots[0] * roots[1]\n\nresult = rs_over_t + st_over_r + tr_over_s\nprint(result)\n```",
