      "text": "Let's denote the polynomial equation as \\( P(x) = x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 \\). The roots of the polynomial are \\( r, s, \\) and \\( t \\).\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[ r + s + t = 5 \\]\n\\[ rs + rt + st = 6 \\]\n\\[ rst = 9 \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( \\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} \\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression in a common denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{rs \\cdot rs + st \\cdot st + tr \\cdot tr}{rst}\n\\]\n\nSince \\( rst = 9 \\), the denominator is simply 9. Now we need to simplify the numerator:\n\\[\nrs \\cdot rs + st \\cdot st + tr \\cdot tr = r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity for the sum of cubes (which shows a relationship between these terms):\n\\[\nr^3 s^3 t^3 = (rst)^3 = 9^3 = 729\n\\]\n\nWe also know:\n\\[\n(r^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2)^2 = (rst)^2 (r^2 s^2 s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2 t^2 + r^2 s^2 r^2) = (rst)^2 \\cdot (1 + 1 + 1) = 3 \\cdot 729 = 2187\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\nr^2 s^2 + s^2 t^2 + t^2 r^2 = \\sqrt{2187} = 27\n\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{27}{9} = 3\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3}\n\\]",
