      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "First, express the roots $r$, $s$, and $t$ as solutions of the equation $x^3-5x^2+6x-9=0$. Using the substitution $i=z+\\ln 9$, we find\n\n$(r-i)(s-i)(t-i)=9$,\n$(r-i)(s-i)=9(1+z)$,\n$(s-i)(t-i)=9(1+z)$,\n$(t-i)(r-i)=9(1+z)$.\n\nNow, these equations are equal to\n\n$9rs=(r-i)(s-i)=9(1+z)$,\n$9st=(s-i)(t-i)=9(1+z)$,\n$9rt=(t-i)(r-i)=9(1+z)$.\n\nAdding these three equations together, we get $9rs+9st+9rt=27(1+z)$. We see that $3(1+z)=27(1+z)$, which simplifies to $3=27$, which is absurd. Therefore. \n\\[\\boxed{0}.\\]",
